This file is tarzan.def, from which is created tarzan.c.  It implements
bbash's "tarzan" builtin: a clearer-interface wrapper around tar, backed
by libarchive so archives are fully standard tar format (with transparent
gzip/bzip2/xz/zstd compression, auto-detected from the archive itself on
read and from the output filename's extension on write) -- files created
by tarzan are byte-compatible with real tar, and real tar/other tools'
archives extract correctly with tarzan.  This is a brand-new builtin name
that does not exist in stock Bash and touches no existing command.

